.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt BSDBT-HELPER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bsdbt-helper
.Nd pair, set up and remove Bluetooth devices for bsdbt
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm @LIBEXECDIR@/bsdbt-helper
.Cm pair Ar address pin Op Ar name
.Nm
.Cm hid Ar address Op Ar name
.Nm
.Cm remove Ar address
.Nm
.Cm disconnect Ar address
.Nm
.Cm power Ar device Cm on | off
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is the part of
.Xr bsdbt 1
and the XFCE panel plugin that needs root.
They run it with
.Xr pkexec 1 ;
the polkit action
.Dq org.bsdbt.helper
allows the user of the active local session without a password, and
nobody else.
Each call does one thing and checks its arguments.
.Pp
.Nm
drives the base system's daemons through their configuration files and
.Xr rc 8 :
.Xr hcsecd 8
answers PIN and link key requests and keeps link keys, and
.Xr bthidd 8
turns HID reports into keyboard and mouse input.
It replaces or removes the entry of one device and keeps the rest of
each file as it is; its own entries carry the comment
.Dq # managed by bsdbt .
It enables the daemons in
.Xr rc.conf 5
when it gives them a device.
.Bl -tag -width disconnect
.It Cm pair
Writes the device with
.Ar pin
to
.Pa hcsecd.conf ,
with
.Xr hcsecd 8
stopped meanwhile so that an old link key is dropped too.
Then it opens a connection to the device and asks for authentication
(HCI Create_Connection and Authentication_Requested):
.Xr hcsecd 8
answers the adapter's PIN request and receives the new link key, and a
SIGHUP makes it save the key to
.Pa /var/db/hcsecd.keys .
When pairing fails, the device's entry is removed again.
.It Cm hid
Reads the device's HID service record over SDP, checks its report
descriptor with
.Xr usbhid 3
as
.Xr bthidd 8
will, writes it to
.Pa bthidd.conf
and restarts
.Xr bthidd 8 ,
which then connects to the device.
.It Cm remove
Disconnects the device and removes it from both daemons and from the
link key file.
.It Cm disconnect
Closes the connection to the device (HCI Disconnect).
.It Cm power
Runs
.Dq service bluetooth start|stop Ar device .
.El
.Pp
After each change
.Nm
writes
.Pa /var/db/bsdbt.devices ,
which everybody may read:
.Pa hcsecd.conf
holds PINs and is readable by root only.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/bluetooth/hcsecd.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/bluetooth/hcsecd.conf
.It Pa /var/db/hcsecd.keys
.It Pa /etc/bluetooth/bthidd.conf
.It Pa /var/db/bthidd.hids
.It Pa /var/db/bsdbt.devices
.It Pa /var/run/bsdbt-helper.lock
one change at a time
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 2 for a usage error, 3 when the device has no
HID service that
.Xr bthidd 8
can use
.Pq Cm hid , No nothing is printed ,
4 when the device refused to pair, 5 when it did not answer.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bsdbt 1 ,
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
.Xr bthidd 8 ,
.Xr hcsecd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An wugq Aq Mt wugq.dev@gmail.com
.Sh BUGS
.Nm
uses the default configuration files and does not read
.Va hcsecd_config
or
.Va bthidd_config
from
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
